Important nuance / uncertainty: whether TorchViz inspects the autograd graph of the forward pass, or the operations of the optimizer step. The question asks about "the gradient graph" of the Adam optimizer. Strictly speaking, the optimizer step is not part of the autograd graph — it's an eager execution of an in-place operation. But TorchViz might be able to visualize a "graph" constructed from the backward pass and optimizer update. This is a major uncertainty: how do we capture the "graph" of the optimizer update? Options:
