## (2) Proposed approach

**Workload choice.** A deliberately small MLP (e.g., 3 hidden layers, width 128) trained a few steps on a tiny synthetic dataset (or, better for isolation, a *pure optimizer micro-workload*: fixed parameter tensors of several shapes + fixed gradients, no forward model). Rationale: optimizer-side graph complexity is per-parameter-tensor, so model scale is irrelevant to the claim; a small/fixed workload keeps the experiment CPU-feasible and lets us sweep parameter shapes (1D/2D/3D, small/large) to show the complexity ratio is stable, not an artifact of one shape.

