 on which all \u00a74 metrics are computable.\n  - *Go/no-go:* **Go** if pass \u2014 note in the report that \"TorchViz output\" is satisfied only via the shared renderer, and flag this as a deviation from the literal question framing. **If (a), (b), and (c) all fail: NO-GO for the main experiment**; report infeasibility and fall back to static source analysis of TorchOpt's fused op (which answers a different, weaker question and is marked as such).\n\n## 4. Metrics\n\n### 4.1 Complexity (structural; deterministic per run)\nPer optimizer step, per parameter tensor, and summed, for each arm:\n- **N** = node count; **E** = edge count.\n- **K** = number of distinct operation types; **H** = Shannon entropy of the op-type distribution (diversity).\n- **D** = longest-path depth of the graph.\n- **P** = count of generic pointwise ops (`mul`, `add`, `pow`, `sqrt`, `div`, `sub` and in-place variants); **R** = count of reduction ops.\n- Primary summary: ratios `N_B/N_A`, `E_B/E_A`, `K_B/K_A` per shape, plus the full sweep table.\n\n### 4.2 Interpretability\n- **Named-block coverage (objective).** The unfused Adam computation decomposes into 5 semantic blocks: (1) m-update, (2) v-update, (3) bias correction, (4) denominator (`sqrt(v)+\u03b5`), (5) parameter update. Annotators (and the LLM, separately) attempt to partition the graph into these named blocks; coverage = fraction of the 5 blocks unambiguously identifiable, and fraction of nodes assigned to a block. Fused expectation: 1 graph node = 1 atomic \"Adam step\" unit; unfused expectation: 15+ generic nodes mapping onto 5 blocks.\n- **Boilerplate reduction (objective).** Fraction of generic pointwise nodes (P) eliminated by fusion: `1 \u2212 P_B/P_A`.\n- **Human readability (subjective; specified procedure, not results).**\n  - *Who:* 3 annotators with PyTorch/ML background (roster recorded), blinded to arm identity; graphs presented in randomized left/right order, rendered identically for both arms.\n  - *Scale:* 7-point 